    "title": "石墨烯 stocks",
    "title_en": "Graphene stocks",
    "content": "Last updated on Sun 24/11/2024 - 17:28\n石墨烯 is a one-atom-thick sheet of 碳 atoms arranged in a honeycomb (hexagons or chicken-wire) crystal lattice. 石墨烯 is the world's strongest and most 导电 材料, and no wonder that researchers and professionals looked into 石墨烯's 潜力 across many 应用, including 传感器, 电池, conductors, displays, 电子, 能源 generation, medicine and more.\nThe commercialization of 石墨烯 is just in its infancy, but already dozens of new companies have been established to develop 石墨烯 based materials, 应用, 石墨烯 生产 processes and other related activities.\nThere are many\ncompanies directly involved with 石墨烯\n. Most of these companies are either private early stage companies or large companies in which 石墨烯 is just one business segment, but some pure-play 石墨烯 companies are public. Below we will list some 潜力 石墨烯 stocks for investors that wish to take part in the 石墨烯 revolution. For a more in-depth analysis of the possibility of investing in 石墨烯, and a complete public companies listing, see our\n石墨烯 投资 Guide\n.\nPure-play 石墨烯 companies\nIn the past few years several 石墨烯 producers and 石墨烯 application developers started trading in stock exchanges around the world - mostly in Australia, Canada and the UK. Here we'll list some of those companies:\nVersarien\n(AIM:VRS) is an advanced materials group leveraging proprietary 技术 to create innovative engineering solutions for its clients in a diverse range of industries - focusing on 石墨烯 materials.\nHaydale\n(AIM:HAYD) is a UK-based supplier of functionalized 石墨烯 and related technologies. Haydale is mostly involved with 石墨烯 复合材料 solutions and 石墨烯-based inks. In 2016 Haydale acquired ACMC, a US-based silicon carbide whisker manufacturer.\nG6 Materials\n(TSX: GGG), formerly known as 石墨烯 3D Lab, focuses on 发展 of high-performance 石墨烯-enhanced materials.\nOther 石墨烯 投资 options\nSeveral large and public companies (such as\nSamsung\n,\nIntel\n,\nNokia\n,\nIBM\nand\nSony\n) are involved in 石墨烯 研究. These companies may be on the forefront of 石墨烯 研究 - especially in high-end fields such as 电子 and photonics - but 石墨烯, even if successful, will probably represent a small portion of their business.\nAnother option is to invest in 石墨烯 生产 equipment.\nAixtron SE\n, for example, is a provider of deposition equipment to the semiconductor 产业 who offers CVD 石墨烯 生产 systems. Aixtron trades in the NASDAQ (ticker:AIXG). US-based\nCVD Equipment Corporation\nalso offers 石墨烯 R&D and 生产 equipment. CVD Equipment trades in the NASDAQ (ticker: CVV).\nInterested in 石墨烯 investing? our\n石墨烯 投资 guide\nincludes detailed information on over a dozen public 石墨烯 companies.\nFurther reading:\n石墨烯-Info's 石墨烯 投资 Guide\nIntroduction to 石墨烯\nGra...\n\n[注: 本内容由自动翻译系统生成,可能存在不准确之处,建议参考原文]",
    "content_en": "Last updated on Sun 24/11/2024 - 17:28\nGraphene is a one-atom-thick sheet of carbon atoms arranged in a honeycomb (hexagons or chicken-wire) crystal lattice. Graphene is the world's strongest and most conductive material, and no wonder that researchers and professionals looked into graphene's potential across many applications, including sensors, batteries, conductors, displays, electronics, energy generation, medicine and more.\nThe commercialization of graphene is just in its infancy, but already dozens of new companies have been established to develop graphene based materials, applications, graphene production processes and other related activities.\nThere are many\ncompanies directly involved with graphene\n. Most of these companies are either private early stage companies or large companies in which graphene is just one business segment, but some pure-play graphene companies are public. Below we will list some potential graphene stocks for investors that wish to take part in the graphene revolution. For a more in-depth analysis of the possibility of investing in graphene, and a complete public companies listing, see our\nGraphene Investment Guide\n.\nPure-play graphene companies\nIn the past few years several graphene producers and graphene application developers started trading in stock exchanges around the world - mostly in Australia, Canada and the UK. Here we'll list some of those companies:\nVersarien\n(AIM:VRS) is an advanced materials group leveraging proprietary technology to create innovative engineering solutions for its clients in a diverse range of industries - focusing on graphene materials.\nHaydale\n(AIM:HAYD) is a UK-based supplier of functionalized graphene and related technologies. Haydale is mostly involved with graphene composite solutions and graphene-based inks. In 2016 Haydale acquired ACMC, a US-based silicon carbide whisker manufacturer.\nG6 Materials\n(TSX: GGG), formerly known as Graphene 3D Lab, focuses on development of high-performance graphene-enhanced materials.\nOther graphene investment options\nSeveral large and public companies (such as\nSamsung\n,\nIntel\n,\nNokia\n,\nIBM\nand\nSony\n) are involved in graphene research. These companies may be on the forefront of graphene research - especially in high-end fields such as electronics and photonics - but graphene, even if successful, will probably represent a small portion of their business.\nAnother option is to invest in graphene production equipment.\nAixtron SE\n, for example, is a provider of deposition equipment to the semiconductor industry who offers CVD graphene production systems. Aixtron trades in the NASDAQ (ticker:AIXG). US-based\nCVD Equipment Corporation\nalso offers graphene R&D and production equipment. CVD Equipment trades in the NASDAQ (ticker: CVV).\nInterested in graphene investing? our\ngraphene investment guide\nincludes detailed information on over a dozen public graphene companies.\nFurther reading:\nGraphene-Info's Graphene Investment Guide\nIntroduction to graphene\nGra...",
