    "content": "Last updated on Thu 04/07/2024 - 07:52\n石墨烯 is a one-atom-thick sheet of 碳 atoms arranged in a honeycomb-like pattern. 石墨烯 is considered to be the world's thinnest, strongest and most 导电 材料 - of both electricity and heat. All of these 性能 are exciting researchers and businesses around the world - as 石墨烯 has the 潜力 to revolutionize entire industries - in the fields of electricity, conductivity, 能源 generation, 电池, 传感器 and more.\n机械 strength\n石墨烯 is the world's strongest 材料, and can be used to enhance the strength of other materials. Dozens of researchers have demonstrated that adding even a trace amount of 石墨烯 to plastics, metals or other materials can make these materials much stronger - or lighter (as you can use a smaller amount of 材料 to achieve the same strength).\nSuch\n石墨烯-enhanced 复合材料 materials\ncan find uses in aerospace, building materials, mobile devices, and many other 应用.\n热 应用\n石墨烯 is the most heat 导电 found to date. As 石墨烯 is also strong and light, it means that it is a great 材料 for making heat-spreading solutions, such as heat sinks or heat dissipation films. This could be useful in both microelectronics (for example to\nmake LED lighting more 高效 and longer lasting\n) and also in larger 应用 - for example 热 foils for mobile devices.\nHuawei's latest smartphones\n, for example, have adopted 石墨烯-based 热 films.\n能源 storage\nSince 石墨烯 is the world's thinnest 材料, it also extremely high surface-area to volume ratio. This makes 石墨烯 a very 有前景的 材料 for use in 电池 and supercapacitors. 石墨烯 may enable\n电池\nand\nsupercapacitors\n(and even fuel-cells) that can store more 能源 - and charge faster, too.\nThe advantages of 石墨烯 电池\nCoatings ,传感器, 电子 and more\n石墨烯 has a lot of promise for additional 应用: anti-corrosion coatings and paints, 高效 and precise 传感器, faster and 高效 电子,\n柔性 displays\n, 高效\n太阳能 panels\n, faster\nDNA sequencing\n, drug delivery, and more.\n石墨烯 is such a great and basic building block that it seems that any 产业 can benefit from this new 材料. Time will tell where 石墨烯 will indeed make an impact - or whether other new materials will be more suitable.\nThe latest 石墨烯 Application news:\nVIVO Defence Services, which provides maintenance services on behalf of the MOD’s Defence Infrastructure Organisation to more than 27,000 military homes in southeast and southwest England, is conducting data-monitored testing at two military housing sites in Fareham, Hampshire, over the next six months. If successful, the 技术, developed by British 公司\nNexGen Heating\n, could be rolled out across additional homes managed by VIVO across the region.\nThe 技术 uses electric 石墨烯 heated paper - a toughened white wallpaper that can be ...\n\n[注: 本内容由自动翻译系统生成,可能存在不准确之处,建议参考原文]",
    "content_en": "Last updated on Thu 04/07/2024 - 07:52\nGraphene is a one-atom-thick sheet of carbon atoms arranged in a honeycomb-like pattern. Graphene is considered to be the world's thinnest, strongest and most conductive material - of both electricity and heat. All of these properties are exciting researchers and businesses around the world - as graphene has the potential to revolutionize entire industries - in the fields of electricity, conductivity, energy generation, batteries, sensors and more.\nMechanical strength\nGraphene is the world's strongest material, and can be used to enhance the strength of other materials. Dozens of researchers have demonstrated that adding even a trace amount of graphene to plastics, metals or other materials can make these materials much stronger - or lighter (as you can use a smaller amount of material to achieve the same strength).\nSuch\ngraphene-enhanced composite materials\ncan find uses in aerospace, building materials, mobile devices, and many other applications.\nThermal applications\nGraphene is the most heat conductive found to date. As graphene is also strong and light, it means that it is a great material for making heat-spreading solutions, such as heat sinks or heat dissipation films. This could be useful in both microelectronics (for example to\nmake LED lighting more efficient and longer lasting\n) and also in larger applications - for example thermal foils for mobile devices.\nHuawei's latest smartphones\n, for example, have adopted graphene-based thermal films.\nEnergy storage\nSince graphene is the world's thinnest material, it also extremely high surface-area to volume ratio. This makes graphene a very promising material for use in batteries and supercapacitors. Graphene may enable\nbatteries\nand\nsupercapacitors\n(and even fuel-cells) that can store more energy - and charge faster, too.\nThe advantages of graphene batteries\nCoatings ,sensors, electronics and more\nGraphene has a lot of promise for additional applications: anti-corrosion coatings and paints, efficient and precise sensors, faster and efficient electronics,\nflexible displays\n, efficient\nsolar panels\n, faster\nDNA sequencing\n, drug delivery, and more.\nGraphene is such a great and basic building block that it seems that any industry can benefit from this new material. Time will tell where graphene will indeed make an impact - or whether other new materials will be more suitable.\nThe latest Graphene Application news:\nVIVO Defence Services, which provides maintenance services on behalf of the MOD’s Defence Infrastructure Organisation to more than 27,000 military homes in southeast and southwest England, is conducting data-monitored testing at two military housing sites in Fareham, Hampshire, over the next six months. If successful, the technology, developed by British company\nNexGen Heating\n, could be rolled out across additional homes managed by VIVO across the region.\nThe technology uses electric graphene heated paper - a toughened white wallpaper that can be ...",
